<title>USA: U.S. CFTC creates international affairs office.</title>
<headline>U.S. CFTC creates international affairs office.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Futures Trading Commission said Wednesday it will launch an office of international affairs later this month to work with international regulators.</p>
<p>Andrea Corcoran, who has served as director of the agency's division of trading and markets since 1982, will head the new office.</p>
<p>CFTC chairwoman Brooksley Born said the new office reflected the growth in international futures exchanges, soaring trading volume around the world and the need for cooperation with other international regulators.</p>
<p>((-- Washington commodities desk, 202-898-8467))</p>
